id: pm-rl-tl1x
title: Benchmarks and eval results with complete provenance
description: "A Benchmark is a versioned suite: tasks, scoring function, pass criteria. An EvalResult is one checkpoint scored against one benchmark version, depending on both the Run that produced the checkpoint and the benchmark version. A Benchmark may also declare a contamination edge to an Environment whose task suite it overlaps, which is what makes the leaderboard's second refusal derivable from the graph."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:38:34.333Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T06:38:34.706Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: An EvalResult depends on both its Run and its Benchmark version; a leaderboard row traces back through the graph to every environment version and reward spec that contributed to it; a contamination edge is a typed dependency rather than a free-text note
